================================================================================
AI CODE DEBUGGER (STREAMLIT + GEMINI) SETUP ON AMAZON LINUX 2
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: LAUNCH EC2 INSTANCE (AWS FREE TIER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Go to AWS Console -> EC2 -> Launch Instance.
2. Name: ai-debugger-app
3. OS / AMI: Select "Amazon Linux 2 AMI (HVM) - Kernel 5.10, SSD Volume Type"
4. Instance Type: t2.micro (Free Tier eligible)
5. Key Pair: Select your .pem key
6. Network Settings (Security Group):
   - SSH (Port 22) -> Anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)
   - Custom TCP (Port 8501) -> Anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)
7. Click "Launch Instance".


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2: CONNECT AND INSTALL PYTHON 3.9 & DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Connect via SSH (Note: Amazon Linux default user is 'ec2-user')
ssh -i "your-key.pem" ec2-user@<YOUR-EC2-PUBLIC-IP>

# 2. Update existing packages
sudo yum update -y

# 3. Install Python 3.9 and Git (Amazon Linux 2 default Python is 2.7/3.7)
sudo amazon-linux-extras enable python3.8 -y || sudo yum install -y python3 python3-pip git
sudo yum install -y python3-devel gcc

# 4. Create project directory and setup virtual environment
mkdir ai-debugger && cd ai-debugger
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# 5. Upgrade pip and install required Python libraries
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install streamlit google-genai


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3: CREATE THE APPLICATION FILE (app.py)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nano app.py

# Paste this exact code into app.py:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
import os
import streamlit as st
from google import genai

st.set_page_config(page_title="AI Code Debugger", layout="centered")

st.title("🐞 AI Code & Error Explainer")
st.write("Paste your broken code or terminal error below to get an instant fix!")

api_key = os.environ.get("GEMINI_API_KEY")
if not api_key:
    api_key = st.sidebar.text_input("Enter Gemini API Key", type="password")

error_input = st.text_area(
    "Your Broken Code or Error Log:",
    height=180,
    placeholder="e.g., IndexError: list index out of range or SQL syntax error..."
)

if st.button("Fix My Bug with AI"):
    if not api_key:
        st.warning("Please provide a Gemini API Key to proceed.")
    elif not error_input.strip():
        st.warning("Please paste some error logs or code first.")
    else:
        with st.spinner("Analyzing with AI..."):
            try:
                client = genai.Client(api_key=api_key)
                prompt = f"""
                You are a senior software engineer helping a student.
                Analyze the following error or broken code snippet:
                
                {error_input}

                Provide a response formatted in Markdown:
                ### 1. What Went Wrong
                Explain the root cause in 2 simple sentences.

                ### 2. Corrected Code
                Provide the full corrected code snippet.

                ### 3. Quick Prevention Tip
                One line on how to avoid this bug in the future.
                """
                response = client.models.generate_content(
                    model='gemini-2.5-flash',
                    contents=prompt,
                )
                st.success("Analysis Complete!")
                st.markdown(response.text)
            except Exception as e:
                st.error(f"Error: {e}")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Press Ctrl+O, hit Enter to save, then press Ctrl+X to exit nano.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4: SETUP SYSTEMD SERVICE (RUNS 24/7 AS EC2-USER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Open a new service file
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/aidebugger.service

# 2. Paste this configuration (Replace YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY with your actual key):
[Unit]
Description=Streamlit AI Debugger Application
After=network.target

[Service]
User=ec2-user
WorkingDirectory=/home/ec2-user/ai-debugger
Environment="PATH=/home/ec2-user/ai-debugger/venv/bin"
Environment="GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY"
ExecStart=/home/ec2-user/ai-debugger/venv/bin/streamlit run app.py --server.port 8501 --server.address 0.0.0.0

Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

# Press Ctrl+O, hit Enter to save, then press Ctrl+X to exit.

# 3. Reload daemon, start and enable service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl start aidebugger
sudo systemctl enable aidebugger

# 4. Check status (should display 'active (running)')
sudo systemctl status aidebugger


